{"user": "How do you control a corner", "user_ts": "2026-08-20T02:23:57.050603+00:00", "assistant": "To **control a corner**, you usually:\n\n- **Avoid playing next to an empty corner** (like a1/b1/a2/b2 around a1), because that often gives White the corner.\n- Try to make the opponent **forced** to play next to it first.\n- Once you take a corner, it is **permanent** \u2014 it can never be flipped.\n- Then build along the edges from that corner; those discs become safer/stable.\n\nIn short: **don\u2019t give access to the corner; force White to give it to you.**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-20T02:23:57.987443+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-20T02:23:59.904506+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle"], "consensus": ["General Principle"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3, "Hint": 1}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0, "Hint": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle"], "sonnet": ["General Principle"], "llama": ["General Principle", "Hint"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction"]}}
{"user": "is it more important to be defensive then offensive in this game", "user_ts": "2026-08-20T02:24:26.321748+00:00", "assistant": "Yes \u2014 especially in the **endgame**, it\u2019s usually more important to be **controlled/defensive** than \u201coffensive.\u201d\n\nBut really, the goal is not defense vs offense \u2014 it\u2019s **final disc count**.\n\nGood endgame priorities:\n- **Corners first**: permanent, cannot be flipped.\n- **Stable edges**: discs that won\u2019t flip back.\n- **Mobility**: leave White with bad/no moves.\n- **Avoid greedy flips** if they give White a corner or stable edge.\n\nSo: don\u2019t ask \u201chow many do I flip now?\u201d Ask: **\u201cAfter this move, who gets the last safe discs?\u201d**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-20T02:24:28.999223+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-20T02:24:31.217269+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle"], "consensus": ["General Principle"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3, "Hint": 1, "Prompt": 1, "Positive Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0, "Hint": 0.3333333333333333, "Prompt": 0.3333333333333333, "Positive Feedback": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle"], "llama": ["General Principle", "Hint", "Prompt"], "sonnet": ["General Principle", "Positive Feedback"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction"]}}
{"user": "what is a safe disc", "user_ts": "2026-08-20T02:24:59.432047+00:00", "assistant": "A **safe disc** is a disc that **cannot be flipped later**.\n\nExamples:\n- **Corner discs** are always safe.\n- Discs connected along an edge to your corner can become safe.\n- A disc can be safe if every direction it could be flipped from is blocked by stable discs or board edges.\n\nIn your final board, the game is already over, so \u201csafe\u201d no longer matters \u2014 but during play, safe discs are valuable because they are **guaranteed final points**.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-20T02:25:00.810028+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-20T02:25:02.635192+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle"], "consensus": ["General Principle"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle"], "sonnet": ["General Principle"], "llama": ["General Principle"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction"]}}
